  "question": {
    "text": "A random variable $X$ has the probability distribution:\n\\begin{array}{|c|c|c|c|c|c|c|c|c|}\n\\hline \\mathrm{X}: & 1 & 2 & 3 & 4 & 5 & 6 & 7 & 8 \\\\\n\\hline \\mathrm{p}(\\mathrm{X}): & 0.15 & 0.23 & 0.12 & 0.10 & 0.20 & 0.08 & 0.07 & 0.05 \\\\\n\\hline\n\\end{array}\nFor the events $E=\\{X$ is a prime number $\\}$ and $F=\\{X < 4\\}$, the probability $P(E \\cup F)$ is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "WMnmr",
      "text": "\n$0.87$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
